(Solar Field Report: Station Meridian-7) Tj
T*
T*
(Section 1 - Power Generation.) Tj
T*
(The primary generator at Station Meridian-7 produces 3.5 kilowatts) Tj
T*
(of continuous power under full sunlight. Output is measured at the) Tj
T*
(main bus and logged every fifteen minutes by the telemetry unit.) Tj
T*
(Peak generation occurs between 10:00 and 14:00 local time, when the) Tj
T*
(panel array is closest to perpendicular with the incident sunlight.) Tj
T*
T*
(Section 2 - Energy Storage.) Tj
T*
(The backup battery bank stores 12 kilowatt-hours and was installed) Tj
T*
(in March 2021 by the maintenance crew led by Dr. Farah Nazari.) Tj
T*
(The bank uses lithium iron phosphate cells rated for 6000 cycles,) Tj
T*
(chosen over lead-acid for their tolerance of deep discharge in the) Tj
T*
(high daytime temperatures the station regularly experiences.) Tj
T*
T*
(Section 3 - Water Purification.) Tj
T*
(Water purification runs on the surplus load and processes up to) Tj
T*
(400 liters of drinking water per day through a two-stage reverse) Tj
T*
(osmosis membrane. The pre-filter is replaced every ninety days,) Tj
T*
(and the crew keeps three spare membranes in the supply locker.) Tj
T*
T*
(Section 4 - Logistics.) Tj
T*
(The nearest resupply depot is 84 kilometers to the north, reachable) Tj
T*
(only during the dry season between May and September. Outside that) Tj
T*
(window the access road floods and deliveries are suspended.) Tj
T*
T*
(Section 5 - Emergency Protocol.) Tj
T*
(If generator output drops below 1 kilowatt, switch to battery-only) Tj
T*
(mode and radio the depot on channel 9. Do not attempt repairs on) Tj
T*
(the array during a dust storm; wait until visibility clears.) Tj
T*
ET
